Package: hsaCEtool
Title: Habitat Selection Analysis Data Preparation for the Caribou Cumulative Effects Tool
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Julie W.", "Turner", email = "jwturner@ualberta.ca",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Steps for a 'targets' pipeline that prepares caribou location
    data and landscape layers for habitat selection analysis (integrated step
    selection analysis, iSSA) behind the caribou cumulative effects tool:
    reading and cleaning GPS locations, building tracks and random steps,
    building disturbance, fire, harvest, land cover, terrain and forest age
    layers (including a merged Yukon disturbance layer), extracting them along
    steps, and fitting the models. Settings are read from layered YAML files so
    one set of code serves many study areas.
